### =============================================================
### Payment Intents — full coverage HTTP test suite
### Covers every endpoint, validation rule, idempotency scenario
### and state-machine transition exposed by
### libs/payments/infra/httpapi/handlers.go +
### libs/payments/infra/idempotency/middleware.go.
###
### Endpoints under test:
###   POST /v1/payment-intents                  (auth + Idempotency-Key)
###   GET  /v1/payment-intents                  (auth, list)
###   GET  /v1/payment-intents/{id}             (auth, detail)
###   POST /v1/payment-intents/{id}/authorize   (auth)
###   POST /v1/payment-intents/{id}/capture     (auth)
###
### State machine: pending → authorized → captured
### Invalid transitions → 409 (mapped from domain.ErrInvalidTransition).
### Idempotent-Replay header is set on cached responses.
### Cross-tenant access yields 404 (tenant isolation silently masks).
###
### Prerequisite: identity.http must be run first (sections 1.1–1.2)
### to seed merchant_id + api_key_token referenced below.
### =============================================================

### Variables
@base_url = http://localhost:8080
@nonexistent_id = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@malformed_uuid = not-a-uuid

### Chained from identity.http bootstrap (run identity.http first)
@api_key_token = {{ issueApiKey.response.body.secret }}

### Idempotency keys — stable per scenario so we can replay deliberately
@idem_key_happy = key-happy-001
@idem_key_replay = key-replay-002
@idem_key_conflict = key-conflict-003

### Chained from this file
@intent_id = {{ createIntent.response.body.id }}
@intent_id_for_capture = {{ createIntentForCapture.response.body.id }}

### =============================================================
### 1. AUTHENTICATION SANITY
### Identity issues the bearer; here we just confirm every Payments
### route returns 401 when the token is missing.
### =============================================================

### 1.1 POST /v1/payment-intents without auth (expect 401)
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: anything

{
    "amount": {"amount_cents": 1000, "currency": "BRL"}
}

### 1.2 GET /v1/payment-intents without auth (expect 401)
GET {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents

### 1.3 GET detail without auth (expect 401)
GET {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents/{{ nonexistent_id }}

### 1.4 POST /authorize without auth (expect 401)
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents/{{ nonexistent_id }}/authorize

### 1.5 POST /capture without auth (expect 401)
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents/{{ nonexistent_id }}/capture

### =============================================================
### 2. CREATE PAYMENT INTENT — happy path
### POST /v1/payment-intents
### Returns 201 + PaymentIntent with status="pending".
### =============================================================

### 2.1 Create with minimum fields (success — pending)
# @name createIntent
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}
Idempotency-Key: {{ idem_key_happy }}

{
    "amount": {"amount_cents": 1990, "currency": "BRL"},
    "card_token": "tok_test_visa_4242",
    "description": "First test intent"
}

### 2.2 Create with description omitted (success)
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}
Idempotency-Key: {{ $guid }}

{
    "amount": {"amount_cents": 5000, "currency": "BRL"},
    "card_token": "tok_test_master_5555"
}

### =============================================================
### 3. CREATE — idempotency middleware
### Header Idempotency-Key required by libs/payments/infra/idempotency.
### - Missing → 400 missing_idempotency_key
### - Same key + same body → cached 201 + header Idempotent-Replay:true
### - Same key + different body → 409 idempotency_conflict
### =============================================================

### 3.1 Create without Idempotency-Key (expect 400 missing_idempotency_key)
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}

{
    "amount": {"amount_cents": 100, "currency": "BRL"},
    "card_token": "tok_x"
}

### 3.2 Create with key (first call — fresh 201)
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}
Idempotency-Key: {{ idem_key_replay }}

{
    "amount": {"amount_cents": 2500, "currency": "BRL"},
    "card_token": "tok_replay"
}

### 3.3 Replay same key + same body (expect 201 + Idempotent-Replay: true)
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}
Idempotency-Key: {{ idem_key_replay }}

{
    "amount": {"amount_cents": 2500, "currency": "BRL"},
    "card_token": "tok_replay"
}

### 3.4 Same key + DIFFERENT body (expect 409 idempotency_conflict)
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}
Idempotency-Key: {{ idem_key_replay }}

{
    "amount": {"amount_cents": 9999, "currency": "BRL"},
    "card_token": "tok_other"
}

### 3.5 Idempotency key reused after error response — fresh attempt allowed
# 4xx responses are NOT persisted by the middleware (only 2xx are saved),
# so a key that previously returned 400 can be used again successfully.
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}
Idempotency-Key: {{ idem_key_conflict }}

{
    "amount": {"amount_cents": 0, "currency": "BRL"},
    "card_token": "tok_will_fail"
}

### 3.6 Same key, valid body (expect 201 — the failed attempt above did not lock the key)
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}
Idempotency-Key: {{ idem_key_conflict }}

{
    "amount": {"amount_cents": 100, "currency": "BRL"},
    "card_token": "tok_ok"
}

### =============================================================
### 4. CREATE — domain validation surface
### Body decoded via contracts.CreatePaymentIntentRequest; amount
### goes through domain.NewMoney which enforces ISO-4217 + sign.
### =============================================================

### 4.1 Malformed JSON (expect 400 invalid_body)
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}
Idempotency-Key: {{ $guid }}

{not-json}

### 4.2 Negative amount (expect 400 invalid_amount)
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}
Idempotency-Key: {{ $guid }}

{
    "amount": {"amount_cents": -100, "currency": "BRL"},
    "card_token": "tok_x"
}

### 4.3 Zero amount (expect 400 invalid_amount — domain rejects ≤ 0)
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}
Idempotency-Key: {{ $guid }}

{
    "amount": {"amount_cents": 0, "currency": "BRL"},
    "card_token": "tok_x"
}

### 4.4 Unknown currency (expect 400 invalid_amount — not in ISO-4217)
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}
Idempotency-Key: {{ $guid }}

{
    "amount": {"amount_cents": 1000, "currency": "XYZ"},
    "card_token": "tok_x"
}

### 4.5 Currency in lower case (expect 400 — domain expects upper-case)
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}
Idempotency-Key: {{ $guid }}

{
    "amount": {"amount_cents": 1000, "currency": "brl"},
    "card_token": "tok_x"
}

### 4.6 Missing card_token (expect 400 — required by contract)
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}
Idempotency-Key: {{ $guid }}

{
    "amount": {"amount_cents": 1000, "currency": "BRL"}
}

### 4.7 Missing amount (expect 400)
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}
Idempotency-Key: {{ $guid }}

{
    "card_token": "tok_x"
}

### =============================================================
### 5. LIST PAYMENT INTENTS
### GET /v1/payment-intents
### Returns the merchant's intents in created_at DESC order.
### Pagination via ?limit= (handler uses strconv on query param).
### =============================================================

### 5.1 Default list (success — should include the intents created in §2 and §3)
# @name listIntents
GET {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}

### 5.2 With small limit (success — capped to the value)
GET {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents?limit=2
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}

### 5.3 With limit=0 (handler treats as "use default")
GET {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents?limit=0
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}

### 5.4 With limit=999999 (handler clamps to repo default cap)
GET {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents?limit=999999
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}

### 5.5 With negative limit (expect 200 — treated as default; handler is lenient)
GET {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents?limit=-1
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}

### 5.6 With non-numeric limit (expect 200 — handler ignores parse failures)
GET {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents?limit=abc
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}

### =============================================================
### 6. GET PAYMENT INTENT BY ID
### GET /v1/payment-intents/{id}
### Tenant-isolated: if the intent exists but belongs to another
### merchant, the handler returns 404 (silent masking — never 403).
### =============================================================

### 6.1 GET existing intent (success)
GET {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents/{{ intent_id }}
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}

### 6.2 GET non-existent UUID (expect 404 not_found)
GET {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents/{{ nonexistent_id }}
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}

### 6.3 GET malformed UUID in path (expect 400 invalid_id)
GET {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents/{{ malformed_uuid }}
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}

### =============================================================
### 7. AUTHORIZE — state machine pending → authorized
### POST /v1/payment-intents/{id}/authorize
### Idempotent: short-circuits if status is already "authorized".
### Invalid transition (e.g. captured → authorize) → 409.
### =============================================================

### 7.1 Authorize a pending intent (success — status flips to authorized)
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents/{{ intent_id }}/authorize
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}

### 7.2 Authorize the same intent again (expect 200 — idempotent short-circuit)
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents/{{ intent_id }}/authorize
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}

### 7.3 Authorize non-existent id (expect 404)
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents/{{ nonexistent_id }}/authorize
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}

### 7.4 Authorize with malformed id (expect 400 invalid_id)
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents/{{ malformed_uuid }}/authorize
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}

### =============================================================
### 8. CAPTURE — state machine authorized → captured
### POST /v1/payment-intents/{id}/capture
### Requires status="authorized". pending → capture short-circuits
### into a 409 invalid_transition.
### =============================================================

### 8.1 Create a second intent to walk the full state machine
# @name createIntentForCapture
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}
Idempotency-Key: {{ $guid }}

{
    "amount": {"amount_cents": 7777, "currency": "BRL"},
    "card_token": "tok_capture_flow",
    "description": "Full-cycle intent for capture test"
}

### 8.2 Try to capture a pending intent (expect 409 invalid_transition)
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents/{{ intent_id_for_capture }}/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}

### 8.3 Authorize it first (success)
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents/{{ intent_id_for_capture }}/authorize
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}

### 8.4 Capture it (success — status flips to captured)
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents/{{ intent_id_for_capture }}/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}

### 8.5 Capture it again (expect 200 — idempotent short-circuit on captured)
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents/{{ intent_id_for_capture }}/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}

### 8.6 Try to authorize a captured intent (expect 409 invalid_transition)
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents/{{ intent_id_for_capture }}/authorize
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}

### 8.7 Capture non-existent id (expect 404)
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents/{{ nonexistent_id }}/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}

### 8.8 Capture with malformed id (expect 400 invalid_id)
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents/{{ malformed_uuid }}/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}

### =============================================================
### 9. AUTH / METHOD ERRORS
### =============================================================

### 9.1 Bogus token on list (expect 401 invalid_credentials)
GET {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents
Authorization: Bearer irk_aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa.bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb

### 9.2 OPTIONS on list (chi default OPTIONS handler — should not require auth)
OPTIONS {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents

### 9.3 HEAD on list (expect 200 — chi auto-maps GET routes to HEAD)
HEAD {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}

### 9.4 PUT on /v1/payment-intents (expect 405 — only GET + POST routed)
PUT {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}

### 9.5 DELETE on a payment intent (expect 405 — destructive ops not exposed)
DELETE {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents/{{ intent_id }}
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}

### 9.6 POST on detail without /authorize|/capture (expect 405)
POST {{ base_url }}/v1/payment-intents/{{ intent_id }}
Authorization: Bearer {{ api_key_token }}
